@* Select (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@
@* The MVC tag helpers are off on this page: the asp-for snippet is shown as text, not compiled against the docs
   page's own model. *@
@removeTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/form.css</code></li>
    <li>No tag helper - the classes are the API</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>Write <code>dnf-select</code> on a native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>. It looks like an
    <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/input">input</a> with the sprite's chevron at the end, drawn in the muted text
    colour of the current theme. Keyboard, screen reader and form behaviour stay the browser's own.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-field max-w-md">
        <label class="dnf-field__label" for="select-status">Status</label>
        <select class="dnf-select" id="select-status">
            <option>Draft</option>
            <option selected>Published</option>
            <option>Scheduled</option>
            <option>Archived</option>
        </select>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="styled-list" title="Styled list" description="Where the browser supports the customizable select (Chromium 135 and later) the open list is a raised card like a dropdown menu, with a check on the chosen row and a chevron that turns while open; other browsers show their native list." layout="block">
