<ui-doc-code id="custom-tokens-css" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-controls :is(.dnf-input, .dnf-select, .dnf-textarea) {
    --dnf-control-height: var(--dnf-control-lg);
    --dnf-control-padding-x: var(--dnf-space-4);
    --dnf-control-font-size: var(--dnf-text-md);
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-select</code></td><td>block</td><td>the input look, <code>appearance: none</code>, the sprite's chevron at the end (the up chevron while the list is open, in browsers with <code>:open</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-select--sm</code> / <code>--lg</code></td><td>size</td><td>30 / 44px high; the small one has a smaller chevron</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-select--auto</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>content width, at least 9rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-select[multiple]</code></td><td>-</td><td>no chevron; stays a native list box</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Inside other components a select is sized for them: in a <code>.dnf-toolbar</code> it is <code>width: auto</code> (at least
    9rem), in a <code>.dnf-bulk-bar</code> at most 16rem, in the pagination's rows-per-page at least 4.5rem.</p>

<h3 id="styled-list-reference">The styled list</h3>
<p>Where the browser supports <code>appearance: base-select</code> (Chromium 135 and later), a single select is drawn by
    the library end to end:</p>
<ul>
    <li>the chevron is the select's <code>::picker-icon</code> and turns 180 degrees while the list is open;</li>
    <li>the list (<code>::picker(select)</code>) is a raised card - <code>--dnf-surface-raised</code>, a border, <code>--dnf-radius-lg</code>, a medium shadow - at least as wide as the select and at most 20rem high, that fades and slides in;</li>
    <li>options are rows like dropdown menu items: hover and focus use <code>--dnf-surface-hover</code>, the chosen one is semibold with a check (<code>::checkmark</code>) at the end, a disabled one is dimmed.</li>
</ul>
<p>Other browsers keep their native list and the background chevron. Multiple selects are never restyled this way.</p>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>hover</td><td><code>:hover</code>, <code>[data-hovered="true"]</code></td><td>darker border</td></tr>
        <tr><td>keyboard focus</td><td><code>:focus-visible</code></td><td><code>--dnf-primary</code> border and the focus ring</td></tr>
        <tr><td>open</td><td><code>:open</code></td><td>the chevron points up</td></tr>
        <tr><td>disabled</td><td><code>:disabled</code>, <code>[aria-disabled="true"]</code></td><td>muted surface and text, no shadow</td></tr>
        <tr><td>invalid</td><td><code>[aria-invalid="true"]</code>, <code>[data-invalid="true"]</code>, <code>.input-validation-error</code>, inside <code>.dnf-field[data-invalid="true"]</code></td><td><code>--dnf-danger</code> border</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="tokens">Tokens</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Set on</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-control-height</code>, <code>--dnf-control-padding-x</code>, <code>--dnf-control-font-size</code></td><td>the select</td><td>size, as on the <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/input#tokens">input</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-select-chevron-size</code></td><td>the select</td><td>the chevron's size (1rem; 0.875rem small)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-select-chevron</code>, <code>--dnf-select-chevron-open</code></td><td><code>:root</code> and every <code>[data-theme]</code></td><td>the chevron images, in each theme's muted text colour - a <code>data-theme</code> subtree gets its own</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>There is no tag helper: the classes above are the API, on a native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> with its own attributes
    (<code>multiple</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>disabled</code>, <code>required</code>) and <code>&lt;option&gt;</code> /
    <code>&lt;optgroup&gt;</code> children. Fill it with <code>asp-items</code> or write the options yourself.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>A native select keeps its keyboard and screen-reader behaviour, also when the list is styled.</li>
    <li>Label it like any control; a filter select in a toolbar gets <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
    <li>Mark an invalid select <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> and link its error with <code>aria-describedby</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/segmented">segmented control</a> or <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/radio">radios</a> for 2 to 4 options that should all be visible.</li>
    <li>Do prefer a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/checkbox">check list</a> to a multiple select for a few options.</li>
    <li>Don't rebuild a select with divs, and don't put rich content in its options - use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/dropdown">dropdown</a> for actions.</li>
</ul>
